  "card": "This PR rewrites the torcontrol fuzz target to route traffic through a mocked DynSock connection to a simulated Tor daemon rather than directly invoking controller callbacks. It synthesizes valid wire replies for PROTOCOLINFO, SAFECOOKIE HMAC challenges, GETINFO, and ADD_ONION, allowing the fuzzer to exercise wire parsing and full handshake success paths. It also fixes a lifetime bug in DynSock::Wait() that caused the socket to delete itself upon return. The author reports line coverage on src/torcontrol.cpp rising from 52% to 81%.",
